On Nov 11, 2007 10:15 AM,  <MorphemeAddict@wmconnect.com> wrote:
> Does Lojban treat logical connectives the same way that Loglan does?

In what sense? The Lojban system is a direct inheritor of the Loglan one,
so they are very smilar, but there are some minor differences. For example,
Loglan uses the A-series not just for sumti connection but also for bridi-tail
connection, it doesn't have Lojban's GIhA.

